# User runs tests and scripts

On this machine, the agent's shell often fails or is aborted. **Do not rely on running pytest, installers, tray launchers, or other project scripts yourself** to verify work.

## What to do instead

1. Make the code/test changes.
2. Tell the user the exact command(s) to run (PowerShell-friendly).
3. Wait for their result — they often paste output or point at `pytest-last.log` (repo root; written by `tests/conftest.py`).
4. Treat `@pytest-last.log` / "passed" / a failure paste as the source of truth.

## Examples

```text
# Ask the user to run:
python -m pytest tests/unit/test_creopdm_agent_log.py -q --tb=short
Get-Content .\pytest-last.log
```

```text
# ❌ BAD — assume your shell pytest succeeded or block waiting on flaky agent terminals
# ✅ GOOD — ship the fix, give the command, iterate from their pytest-last.log
```

Still use file tools freely. Prefer short, copy-pasteable commands over multi-step shell pipelines the agent would normally chain.
